📌 Real-Time Gesture Translator and Learning Platform for Hearing and Speech Impaired
📖 Project Overview

This project, “Real-Time Gesture Translator and Learning Platform for Hearing and Speech Impaired”, is a Final Year Engineering Project developed as part of the Bachelor of Technology (B.Tech) in Information Technology.

The system uses Computer Vision and Deep Learning techniques to recognize sign language hand gestures in real time and translate them into text and speech output.
Additionally, it provides an interactive learning platform for users to learn and practice sign language, promoting inclusivity and accessibility.

🎯 Objectives
To recognize hand gestures in real time using a webcam
To translate ASL gestures into text and speech
To provide a learning module for non-signers to learn sign language
To bridge the communication gap between hearing-impaired and non-signers
To build a user-friendly and low-cost assistive solution

🧠 Technologies Used
Programming Language: Python 3.10
Libraries & Frameworks:
OpenCV
MediaPipe
TensorFlow / Keras
Tkinter (GUI)
pyttsx3 (Text-to-Speech)
IDE: PyCharm

Platform: Desktop (Windows)

🗂️ Project Structure
PythonProject6/
│
├── recordings_demonstrations/   # Recorded demo videos for lessons (not uploaded)
├── recordings_practice/         # User practice recordings (not uploaded)
├── uploaded_lessons/            # Teacher uploaded lessons (not uploaded)
│
├── .gitignore                   # Git ignore configuration
├── asl.py                       # Core ASL gesture recognition logic
├── main.py                      # Main application entry point
├── asl_users.db                 # User database (login & roles)
├── A.h5                         # Trained CNN model (may be excluded if large)
└── README.md                    # Project documentation

⚠️ Important Note (Files Removed)

Some folders and files have been intentionally removed from this GitHub repository due to large file size and video content restrictions, including:

🎥 recordings_demonstrations/

🎥 recordings_practice/

🎥 uploaded_lessons/

🧠 Large trained model files (.h5) if exceeding GitHub size limits
👉 These files exist locally in the PyCharm project and were used during development, testing, and evaluation, but are not uploaded to GitHub to comply with repository size constraints.

🧪 Features
✅ Real-Time Gesture Recognition
Captures live video through webcam
Detects hand landmarks using MediaPipe\
Classifies gestures using CNN
Displays recognized letters instantly

🔊 Text-to-Speech Translation
Converts recognized gestures into voice output
Enables real-time communication with non-signers

📚 Learning Platform
Structured lessons for ASL alphabets
Practice mode with live feedback
Teacher–Student role-based access
🖥️ Graphical User Interface

Built using Tkinter
Simple, intuitive, and accessible UI
Supports word formation and sentence building

🧪 Performance

Average Accuracy: ~92–93%
Latency: < 0.5 seconds
FPS: 24–28

Works under:
Normal lighting
Moderate background variations

🚀 How to Run the Project
Clone the repository:
git clone https://github.com/ShreyaDhote/Final-Year-Project.git
Install required libraries:
pip install opencv-python mediapipe tensorflow keras pyttsx3
Run the application:
python main.py
⚠️ Ensure a working webcam is connected before running.

🧩 Limitations
Supports static ASL alphabets (A–Z) only
Sensitive to very low lighting conditions
Desktop-based (mobile version planned)
No continuous sentence-level gesture recognition yet

🔮 Future Scope
Dynamic gesture & sentence recognition (LSTM / RNN)
Android mobile application (TensorFlow Lite)
Multilingual speech output
Cloud-based model inference
Integration with IoT and wearable devices
Facial expression & body pose recognition


